{"agent_id":"pp3g-kkmy-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-3645","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:25:16.163683654Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a518ea6a-b72d-4e49-8527-17905ed6c476","comment_uuid":"b995a2e5-15b6-466b-b749-7207e579a29e","author":"pp3g-kkmy-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-3645","content":"VERDICT: CONDITIONAL (release-blocked on the CRITICAL CWD defect + the MAJOR items below)\n\nThe implementation is substantially complete and logically correct for the in-project execution path: the test suite at main HEAD yields 96/98 green (the 2 failures are the non-hermetic T16, which itself exposes the critical CWD defect), and F1-F6 are all present. However it MUST NOT be deployed as documented until the CRITICAL defect and the MAJOR gaps below are fixed. The logic is sound; the blockers are bounded and fixable.\n\n== FINDINGS ==\n\nF1. CRITICAL — All crosslink invocations depend on launch CWD; they silently no-op outside the project.\nEvidence: post_comment L501 `run([\"crosslink\",\"issue\",\"comment\",...])`; kickoff_cleanup L837 `run([\"crosslink\",\"kickoff\",\"cleanup\",...])`; kickoff_stop L854; admission_checks L2261 `run([\"crosslink\",\"issue\",\"show\",issue])`, L2269 `run([\"crosslink\",\"locks\",\"check\",issue])`; last_hub_position L764. None cd to the repo.\nDemonstrated: `crosslink issue show 460` => rc=0 from project root, rc=1 \"Not a crosslink repository (or any parent)\" from /tmp. The documented deployment `tmux new-session -d -s observer-mgr bash …/observer.sh` inherits the launcher CWD. Consequence in real deployment: cleanup, kill, evidence comments, admission alerts, and hub-position all fail — the core supervisor functions are inert. Fix: `cd \"$OB_REPO_ROOT\"` in the bash wrapper after discovery (or pass a repo flag / set CROSSLINK repo env).\n\nF2. MAJOR — Terminal phase is recorded BEFORE the mutation is confirmed, so transient failures are never retried.\nEvidence: act_frozen L1124-1129 sets `rec[\"phase\"]=\"frozen-handled\"` regardless of `kickoff_stop`/`kickoff_cleanup` return; act_killed L1090-1094 same; act_completed L949-967 same. Next cycle the LIKELY-FROZEN/DEAD-UNMARKED branch is skipped because phase is already terminal. If the kill/cleanup was blocked by the 24/hr circuit breaker (plausible in a large swarm) or timed out, the agent is marked handled and NEVER re-killed/re-cleaned. The core safety function can be permanently defeated by a transient breaker block.\n\nF3. MAJOR — Slug-substring attribution collision in agent_log_section.\nEvidence: L538-539 primary `directory=[^\\t ]*<esc>` and L542 fallback `cwd=[^\\t ]*<esc>` where `esc=re.escape(agent)`. A shorter slug (e.g. `zzz-lc`) matches the directory path of a longer slug (`zzz-lc-done`), stealing its session IDs. Wrong evidence is attached to the wrong agent, and rate-limit/death classification can be mis-attributed. Fix: anchor to a path component, e.g. `directory=[^\\t ]*/(zzz\\-lc)(?=\\s|$)`.\n\nF4. MAJOR — LIKELY-FROZEN triggers an immediate destructive kill with no independent aliveness re-check and no observer-side 2-cycle confirmation.\nEvidence: process_agent LIKELY-FROZEN branch L1290-1298 calls act_frozen on the FIRST occurrence (guards only on phase/rate_limited). act_frozen L1117-1157 calls kickoff_stop (kill) WITHOUT first calling pane_status to confirm the pane is not alive. Contrast DEAD-UNMARKED, where classify_death L1039-1055 DOES independently verify pane status. Design requires \"LIKELY-FROZEN confirmed across >= 2 cycles\" (#460 / lifecycle-design.md). A single misclassification by the (out-of-scope) liveness scanner yields an immediate kill of a possibly-healthy agent. Add an observer-side 2-cycle counter and/or a `pane_status != \"alive\"` gate before kill.\n\nF5. MAJOR — Unhandled Python exception in main() discards all in-memory state, causing re-firing of transition actions.\nEvidence: main() L2319-2437 calls save_state only at L2424. Any exception earlier (compose_transition_evidence, agent_log_section, wave_backup, etc.) aborts with empty summary; bash logs `cycle-program-failed` (L2481) but state is NOT persisted. Next cycle re-processes the same verdicts and re-fires act_* (comments/kills); only the 24/hr breaker and admission fingerprinting limit the blast. No try/except wraps main(). Wrap main() so state is always saved (best-effort) before exit.\n\nF6. MAJOR — /tmp/opencode/observer-state tamper surface + symlink vulnerability.\nEvidence: `mkdir -p \"$OBSERVER_STATE_DIR/evidence\"` L300 with default perms; save_state writes STATE_FILE+\".tmp\" via `open(tmp,\"w\")` L461 (follows symlinks); evidence bundles written world-readable under /tmp. Any local user can read sensitive log tails, modify manager-state.json to mark agents `handled` (suppressing kills/cleanup), or pre-create STATE_FILE.tmp as a symlink to a privileged file (arbitrary overwrite via os.replace). Fix: chmod 700 the state dir; use os.open with O_EXCL/O_NOFOLLOW or a per-run secure temp; restrict evidence perms.\n\nF7. MAJOR — Backup pass stamps last_run_ts at START; a failed pass is not retried for a full interval, violating data-retention \"extraction-before-pruning\".\nEvidence: L1971-1976 sets `bk[\"last_run_ts\"]=time.time()` before work; on failure (disk full, store missing, RED verify) the watermark is held (L2067-2074) but last_run_ts already advanced, so the next attempt is BACKUP_INTERVAL_MINS (default 1440=24h) away. A daily backup that fails is silently skipped for 24h. Stamp last_run_ts only after a successful pass (or add a shorter retry-on-failure backoff).\n\nF8. MAJOR — F4 export is schema-dependent and unverified against the real store; silent zero-export possible.\nEvidence: snapshot_session_tables L1827-1841 only matches tables literally named `session`/`session_v2` with columns {id,directory,title,time_created,time_updated}. If the live opencode.db/opencode-fork-pp3g.db uses different names/columns, no table matches, the export loop never runs, and the pass appears to \"succeed\" (no GREEN/RED, no error). Cannot verify the live schema from this review (agent-liveness.py / session-union.py out of scope), so this is a latent data-retention gap. Add an explicit \"no session table found\" error/RED entry.\n\nF9. MAJOR — rclone remote read-back verifies only the index, not the exported artifacts.\nEvidence: rclone_sync_and_verify L1950-1962 reads back only `index/<label>.ndx` via `rclone cat`; the gzip export artifacts are copied (L1944-1949) but never read-back-verified remotely. data-retention.md requires destination-side read-back of the artifacts (row count + sha256). Remote export artifacts could be corrupt/missing undetected.\n\nF10. MINOR/MAJOR — Hardcoded `main` branch.\nEvidence: deliverable_check L914 `merge-base main branch`, L932 `merge-base --is-ancestor branch main`; wave_merge L1354 `refs/heads/main`, L1365 `origin/main`; worktree_git_evidence L743 `git diff --stat main`. Repos with a different default branch silently mis-report merged/deliverable and miss push-ahead alerts. Make the base branch configurable.\n\nF11. MINOR — python-stderr.log captures tracebacks (L2475) but they are never surfaced to events.jsonl; on cycle-program-failed only the fact is logged, not the cause, hampering diagnosis.\n\nF12. MINOR — Unbounded growth: events.jsonl (L431 append, never rotated), model-evidence-staging.jsonl (L878), verification.log/sync-pending.log/prune-report.txt (append-only), and per-transition evidence folders under EVIDENCE_ROOT (one new timestamped dir per terminal transition, L695) accumulate without pruning. Over a long-lived observer this grows without bound.\n\nF13. MINOR — state[\"agents\"] is never pruned (L2339-2355 only flag/relabel, never delete); agent records accumulate in manager-state.json for the life of the observer.\n\nF14. MINOR — wave_admission runs the full admission check (2 crosslink calls/agent + catalog) EVERY cycle for every tracked agent (L2290-2313), including long-term preserved (failed) worktrees; heavy crosslink load and rate-limit exposure for no state change (only alerts are deduped).\n\nF15. MINOR — Test T16 is not hermetic: it asserts issue-exists/issue-claimed `ok:true` against LIVE crosslink #460, which only holds when the observer is launched from a crosslink project dir AND #460 is locked by the session. In this independent run (launched from /tmp) both failed (96/98), proving the CWD dependence (F1) and that the admission issue-exists/claimed paths are unverified in isolation. The builder's 98/98 was an artifact of running from the project root.\n\nF16. MINOR — Fragile CLI-output string parsing: issue-claimed `claimed = rc2==0 and \"is locked by\" in (out2 or \"\")` L2271; working_issue `**Issue**:\\s*#(\\d+)` L651; last_hub_position timestamp regex L769. Any wording change in crosslink output flips agents to \"not claimed\"/wrong issue, causing false admission-violation storms or mis-routed comments.\n\nF17. MINOR — verify_export_readback counts rows via `chunk.count(b\"\\n\")` L1909; safe only because every record ends with `\\n` and JSON contains no embedded newlines — a fragile invariant not asserted; a future record-format change would silently miscount.\n\nF18. (Assumption/risk) — The observer's agent-identity model assumes the liveness scanner emits the worktree directory slug as `agent` (used in WORKTREES_ROOT/agent/... probes at L648, 669, 732, 942, etc.). If agent-liveness.py emits session IDs or tmux names, all worktree-relative probes silently mis-resolve (working_issue->None->comments to FLAG_ISSUE; branch/commit probes->None). Cannot verify without agent-liveness.py (out of scope).\n\n== WHAT WAS DELIVERED (completeness vs spec) ==\n- F1 evidence-at-transition: present and wired into all five terminal actions (act_completed/failed/killed/frozen/finished_unmarkable) with sha256 manifest + digest comment. PASS (logic).\n- F2 fast path: byte-offset cursor, classification (PARKED-RETRYING/CONSENT-GATE-FATAL/RETRY-EXHAUSTED-DEAD/UNKNOWN), same-cycle fire, dedup. PASS (logic).\n- F3 commit-age: commit_age_min feeds STALE escalation + commit-overdue events. PASS (logic).\n- F4 dual-store backup: hot .backup, integrity+sha256, gen cap, incremental export from snapshot, GREEN/RED read-back, prune-gate report, rclone-optional. PASS with schema/retry caveats (F7,F8,F9).\n- F5 admission: model/issue/claim/estimate checks + events.jsonl audit + deduped alerts, no plugin files. PASS with CWD/hermeticity caveats (F1,F15,F16).\n- F6 wave-anomaly: all-agents-vanish platform-restart alert, scan-based re-arm, dedup. PASS (logic).\n\n== WHY ==\nThe architecture and per-feature logic are correct and well-tested in-project, but the supervisor is not safe to run as documented: every crosslink mutation silently fails outside the project directory (F1, CRITICAL), and several MAJOR gaps (F2 retry, F4 kill-without-confirmation, F5 state-loss, F6 tamper) undermine the reliability/safety guarantees the spec exists to provide.\n\n== WHAT ==\nBased on: (a) full source read of observer.sh (2489 lines) + run-tests.sh (528 lines) at main HEAD; (b) the #460 consolidated dispatch spec (F1-F6) and lifecycle-design.md and data-retention.md; (c) empirical execution of the suite at main HEAD (96 passed, 2 failed) and live probing of `crosslink issue show`/`locks check` from project vs /tmp (rc 0 vs 1).\n\n== HOW-CERTAIN ==\nEvidence-based for F1 (demonstrated rc=1 outside project; T16 cascade reproduced), F2/F3/F4/F5/F6 (direct code reading with file:line), F15 (reproduced 2-test failure). High confidence on all numbered items. F8 and F18 are explicitly uncertain (depend on out-of-scope agent-liveness.py / live DB schema).\n\n== WHAT-NOT-TESTED ==\n- Non-dry-run mutations end-to-end (kickoff cleanup/stop against a real fleet) — the suite is dry-run only; the CWD defect (F1) means even dry-run comment paths are unverified outside the project.\n- Real rclone remote sync positive path (no remote wired) — only the negative/pending gate is exercised.\n- RED verification branch not fault-injected (code path inspected only).\n- Long-duration loop behavior with real interval gating and a multi-GB live store.\n- The actual opencode.db / opencode-fork-pp3g.db session-table schema (F8) and agent-liveness.py verdict correctness (F4, F18) — both out of the reviewed file set.","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:25:16.155968489Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:8n785oNkGs4AGsb8PAWg3EJr8KK3VqS1jlP+Ipg1unI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgH9o9t7f7oVLEWsH0nHEu1vSOzCheJ6g+mgfbVfy68HsAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAuNoUw5wzlPbmtM+ZE/ysKEUReql/286N3CVyj/tIRKcV0CAJZuWY7Kj02TYzlIRIwmLZLgq0mwIS/yV4W3dhDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:8n785oNkGs4AGsb8PAWg3EJr8KK3VqS1jlP+Ipg1unI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgH9o9t7f7oVLEWsH0nHEu1vSOzCheJ6g+mgfbVfy68HsAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEhyx+/II7OKqkwXKgGN/yB4ro52ucJfnxr3SGbe08juIFtKLCIr5xZ578A7Ipvj4/WawXcFBb6pFEuj9IaDyQk="}
